# Single-disc fields and movies

Single-disc ships as **one Disc 1 image**. CSR (and other multi-disc sources) can
still have **different** `FIELD/*.DAT` on Disc 1 vs Disc 2 for the same map name.

## Never assume byte size or compressed diff = gameplay change

- Always **LZS-decompress** FIELD DATs before judging content.
- Use `python3 scripts/compare_field_dat.py` (opcodes, sections, dialog content vs padding).
- Extract/install maps: `extract_field_dat.py` / `put_field_dat.py` (not one-off ISO code).
- Classifications: `identical` | `pad-only` (safe) vs `scripts` | `sections` | `mixed` (real).
- Compressed-layer hunks alone are noise (see DEL1 D2 pad-only false alarm).
- Tool index: `scripts/README.md`. Tooling rule: `tooling-standards.mdc`.

## Multi-disc CSR map names (as of 2026-08-06)

Ten maps edited on both CSR D1 and D2 with **different** CSR bytes — all ten are
real script diffs D1 vs D2. Prefer list: `mods/single-disc/patches/csr-field-disc-prefer.txt`.

Batch: `python3 scripts/compare_field_dat.py --batch-collisions`  
Reports: `docs/findings/field-collisions-2026-08-06/`.

When building the Disc 1 image, **choose which disc’s CSR file** lands for each
shared map (or hand-merge). Do not let a later D2/D3 copy silently overwrite a
D1 CSR trim (DEL1 #441 regression).

