## Movies / CD seeks

- Some FMV paths seek **absolute ISO LBA**, not only `MOVIE_ID` (LOSLAKE1 → LBA 250450).
- FMV inject: prefer **raw Mode2 Form2 (2352)** sectors when stream must match hardware/DS.
- Path-critical FMVs (PARASHOT, NRCRL, NRCRLB, METEOFIX, METEOSKY) need **unique EOF LBAs**
  after manip-movies — never share LBA with JAIROFAL/CANONON aliases.
- **Apply order (builder ranks):** manip-movies (10) → single-disc-on-* (20) → endings (30).
  SD core layers are bin-diffed vs CSR+movies; do not reverse that order when shipping.
- **Manip-movies packs:** each new version is **cumulative** (includes all prior movie work).
  Only the **latest** id is `enabled` + `autoIncludeWhen`. Older versions may remain in
  `builder/` / manifest but disabled, same `exclusiveGroup` (`single-disc-csr-movies`).
  Never stack two movie pack versions on one build.
- Playtest entry: `python3 mods/single-disc/scripts/build_playtest_bin.py` → only open
  `workspace/iso-extract/ff7_d1_playtest_csr_sd_movies.cue`.

## Regression tests (required on every single-disc / builder change)

When you change single-disc packs, movie inject, prefer-list, `apply_layer`, builder
apply rank, or EDC repair:

1. **Add or extend a test** under `tests/` that would have failed before the fix
   (unit if possible; integration in `tests/test_single_disc_stack.py` for disc stacks).
2. Run before publish:
   - `python3 -m pytest tests/ -q -m "not integration"` (always)
   - `python3 -m pytest tests/ -q -m integration` (when pristine/CSR bins available)
3. Do **not** ship a new `single-disc-on-csr-v*` if integration fails.
4. Suite index: `scripts/README.md`; ship skill: `ship-single-disc`.

Locked regressions include: LOSIN2/LOST2/CANON_2 prefer, waterfall LBA 250450,
FSHIP_12 PARASHOT, MD8_5/52 NRCRL*, path FMV unique LBAs, endings non-clobber,
2352 image align, EDC Form2/XA skip, movies-before-SD rank.

## Bump `version` on every layer content change

The builder caches layer JSON in IndexedDB keyed by `id@version` (see
`individualcontributordev.github.io/builder/builder.js` `layerContentKey`).
If a layer file's **bytes** change but `builder/manifest.json`'s `version`
field for that pack does not, returning users' browsers keep serving the
**stale cached layer** indefinitely — the CDN can be fully updated and it
won't matter. This caused a false "still broken" report after the row
47/52 audio-flicker fix (2026-08-18) because `single-disc-on-csr` stayed at
`0.1.2` while its layer file changed underneath it.

**Rule:** any time `single-disc-on-csr` (or any other pack)'s layer JSON
content changes, bump its `version` string in `builder/manifest.json` in
the same commit (e.g. `0.1.2` → `0.1.2.1` for a content-only patch, or a
full minor/major bump for a real release). Never ship a layer fix without
a version bump — it will not reach existing users without a manual
"clear pack cache" or the ~stale IndexedDB entry.

## Instructions language

In `docs/INSTRUCTIONS.md` and chat: **plain English** — map file name, which disc’s
CSR file, why. No jargon like “stem”. No “do not use X” lists when “put Y on the
image because …” is enough. One field (or one atomic ops task) per instructions pass.
